’E sulloge me titlo "Ti pathos ateleioto" tou Thoma Korobine (apo to omonumo baru zeimpekiko tou Markou) apoteleitai apo eikosipente aphegematika keimena, to kathena me xekhoristo uphos kai periekhomeno.
Dramatikes kai skamprozikes istories pou diadramatizontai ste Thessalonike, ten Konstantinoupole kai te Mutilene, kai merika mikroteres ektases keimena pou sunduazoun to diegema me to dokimio, denontai m' ena noero nema me aphegemata opou protagonistoun agapemena prosopa-semeia anaphoras tou suggraphea ap' ton khoro tes tekhnes, me idiaitere emblematikoteta kai prosopiko mutho to kathena Bambakares - Kazantzides - Polu Panou - Ntantonake - Rasoules - Papazoglou - Takhtses - Zatele - Mente).
Ta perissotera keimena sterizontai se mia sodeia biomaton tou suggraphea kai apoteloun atophia kommatia authentikes zoes metousiomena se peza.
Periekhomena:
1. Thessalonike, mana mou
2. To moukhampeti
3. Nephokokkozomon
4. Ti kanei e theia Eirene;
5. Nai e okhi;
6. Enteka khiliades berges
7. E phatne tes <>
8. Kalenukhta, karntase mou
9. Na m' ekheis panta opos eimai tora
10. Ksedipsontas sten eremo (Phleru)
11. Skholia pano se mia photographia
12. Ti pathos ateleioto
13. Den tragoudesa Mpagiantera
14. O Stelios sta oneira mou
15. E parthenia tes Eustratias
16. Lesbies kai lesbies
17. E Theatrina
18. Ena gramma ston Kosta Takhtse
19. E Zuranna xorkizei to pneuma tou thanatou
20. Mpok kai Oumit
21. To bouno
22. E gephura tou Peristeriou
23. O thesauros tou Sakat-pazari
24. O Alekos ap' ton Bolo
25. <>
Ena protokhroniatiko paramuthi
Eukharisties"Ÿ
œVon den Jahren des Exils bis ins Wendejahr '89 und daruber hinaus reicht diese wechselvolle Geschichte einer deutschen Familie. Sie fuhrt von Mexiko uber Sibirien bis in die neu gegrundete DDR, fuhrt uber die Gipfel und durch die Abgrunde des 20. Jahrhunderts. So entsteht ein weites Panorama, ein grosser Deutschlandroman, der, ungeheuer menschlich und komisch, Geschichte als Familiengeschichte erlebbar macht."ª
§Pezographos kai demosiographos, ekprosopos tou ethographikou diegematos, o Ioannes Kondulakes perigraphei me monadiko tropo ten istoria enos morphomenou anthropou, pou analambanei tukhaia kai me elaphra te kardia to rolo tou daskalou se ena oreino khorio tes Kretes. Kurio melema tou, protarkhika, einai to kunegi sta kontina dase tes periokhes, ste sunekheia omos ton kerdizei ex oloklerou to epaggelma tou.
Ena biblio sto opoio, me khioumoristiko tropo, diaphainontai ta prota semadia tes paidagogikes methodou pou epharmosteke sto neosustato elleniko kratos.
E agape tou suggraphea gia ten Krete kai tous anthropous tes apokaluptetai kai apo ta idia tou ta logia: "Den gnorizo mepos me parasurei polu e agape mou pros auton ton topon, all' einai bebaion oti kaneis epainos den mou phainetai uperbolikos.""±
®E k. Mpantru xupnontas biaia apo ten eisodo tes kamarieras tes, tha akouge ten pio apisteute eidese. Mesa ste bibliotheke tou Gkossigkton Khol, uperkhe to ptoma mias agnostes neas kopelas, me platinenia mallia, pesmeno orizontia pano sto dermatino khali mprosta sto tzaki. Phorouse asemenia sandalia kai ta nukhia ton podion tes etan bammana me skouro kokkino khroma.
E amphibolia edose te these tes sten abebaioteta, mono otan o suntagmatarkhes Mantru tha eblepe me ta idia tou ta matia to ptoma tes agnostes xanthes kai tha telephonouse khoris kathusterese, sto astunomiko tmema, opou e eidese xaphniase kai ton astunomiko Polk, lagoniko tes topikes astunomias.
Omos, oso ki an e k. Mparnu pisteue sta oneira, allo toso pisteue kai stis xekhoristes ikanotetes tes philes tes mis Marl-kai s' auto den epephte exo."Ã
ÀO Fabien Marsaud (1977), gnostos me to pseudonumo Grand Corps Malade, einai enas apo tous demophilesterous gallous kallitekhnes (tragoudopoios, autoskhediastikos poietes). Gia to kallitekhniko tou ergo ekhei labei plethos diakriseon, eno to 2008 timetheke apo te gallike kubernese me ton titlo tou ippote tou Tagmatos ton Tekhnon kai ton Grammaton.
To kalokairi tou 1997 ergazotan se mia athletike kataskenose kai ekane mia boutia sten pisina, e opoia statheke moiraia gia ten exelixe tou: traumatise polu sobara te spondulike tou stele kai e diagnose etan oti den tha mporouse na perpatesei xana. Ostoso ustera apo enan khrono entatikes therapeias kai epimones prospatheias, diepseuse tis problepseis.
Se auto to biblio aphegeitai me khioumor, peripaiktike diathese kai polu sunaisthema te dodekamene peripeteia tou os atelous tetraplegikou metapherontas mas tis empeiries toso tis dikes tou oso kai ton omoiopathon suntrophon tou apo to Kentro Apokatastases."Æ
ÃEna biblio-stathmos, e sugklonistike marturia tou demosiographou kai istorikou Joachim Fest (Gioakhim Phest) gia to pos perase ten paidike tou elikia ste nazistike Germania os gios enos arnete tou nazismou. To khroniko tes zoes mias oikogeneias pou den sunergasteke me to nazistiko kathestos, pou matose gia na diaphulaxei tis arkhes kai tis axies tes, sugkrouomene me ton komphormismo kai te barbaroteta.
O mikros Gioakhim thumatai oti o pateras tou to 1933, ligo meta ten anodo tou Khitler sten exousia, okhi mono ekhase te douleia tou os polemios tou kathestotos, alla tou apagoreuteke en genei e opoiadepote ergasia. Apo tote e oikogeneia Phest arkhise na antimetopizei sobara problemata, ta geumata eginan polu lita, ta roukha arkhisan na mpalonontai, oi philoi araiosan tis episkepseis tous kai sto skholeio autos kai ta aderphia tou etan daktulodeiktoumenoi - o idios o Gioakhim apobletheke kathos kharasse karikatoures tou Khitler sto thranio tou.
Otan kapoia stigme e metera tou Gioakhim espase kai zetese apo ton antra tes na allaxei gnome kai na graphtei sto Ethnikososialistiko Komma, giati e analetheia etan anekathen to oplo tou aplou kosmou apenanti stous iskhurous, ekeinos tes apantese: "Emeis den eimaste o aplos kosmos. Okhi se tetoia zetemata!"
Mia autobiographike aphegese, grammene ston ruthmo mias melagkholikes mousikes domatiou, pou apotuponei mia epokhe kai anadeiknuei to portreto enos anthropou pou e ethike tou akeraioteta aphupnizei kai empneei."É

Æ
"Oi alaniaredes" einai to pio olokleromeno ergo tou Boutura sten kategoria tes "aletographias" e "tabernographias", opos onomastheke. Ostoso, to plaisio tou ergou den einai ta perithoriaka stromata opos phainetai ek protes opseos, alla oloklero to elleniko proletariato tes protes eikosaetias tou aiona mas, pou etan enas kosmos reustos kai asaphes sto esoteriko tou. Ste noubela o Bouturas apotuponei se proto epipedo ten perirreousa atmosphaira tes mpoemikes argoskholias, alla uphainei tautokhrona sto phonto kai "denei" me ten istoria tou ta kuria kharakteristika tes koinonikes pragmatikotetas ton arkhon tou aiona: oi ornithes sto phtokhospito pou tha khresimeusoun os teleutaia ephedreia diatrophes, to mesitiko grapheio pou den ekhei prosphora ergasias, to ergatiko kapheneio kai "o ergatikos" pou pairnei "mikrodouleies ergolabia", e misobiomekhanike epokhiake ergasia tou eroa, o kheimonas pou ste diarkeia tou "oi douleies kleinane...", e prooptike tes metanasteuses, klp.
O ploutos ton "Alaniaredon" mporei na sunopsistei sto gegonos oti o Bouturas kataphere na eggrapsei ton psukhismo kai tis pio mikres apokhroseis tes anthropines atomikotetas, ten idiaiteroteta ton opoion den anairei e uparxiake genikoteta tes phtokheias, mesa se mia koinonike toikhographia, tes opoias ten pistoteta den anairei e upainiktike skiagraphese tes. [...]"Ï
ÌPote den phantazotan e kharitomene Kate, otan katebaine ston Peiraia na paralabei apo to ploio ton exadelpho tes -kai pithanos mnestera tes-, ton Niku, oti ta xantha tou mallia kai to moustaki tou tha eikhan tetoiou eidous epiptoseis sten anemele zoe tes. Oute omos kai o Kuriakos Kanistrakes, idioktetes kai dieuthuntes tes megales ephemeridas "Prokhoreite!" etan dunaton na dianoethei oti e epophelestate mnesteia tou me ten polupherne Tzitze Zermpine apeileito apo to gegonos oti statheke liga lepta parapano sto parathuro tou, khazeuontas ten kinese ste Stadiou. Ola omos etan na ta perimenei kaneis se mia mikre khora pou paskhize na kratethei oudetere sta 1916, eno guro tes mainotan o A Pagkosmios Polemos, oi kataskopoi energousan pleon sta phanera kai oi ephemerides eikhan oles exagorastei. Mia palaia istoria me epikairous apoekhous."Ó
ĞDen pephteis kathe mera pano s' enan gumno antra sten akre tou dromou. Gi' auto, exallou, e serbitora Souki Stakkhaouz den ton prosperase etsi apla. Kata ta phainomena, to phtokho plasma den eikhe ten paramikre idea poios etan[?] eikhe, omos, e Souki. Etan o Erik to Bampir - ma tora einai enas Erik pio eugenikos, pio kalosunatos. Alla phobismenos sunama, aphou opoios tou eikhe aphairesei te mneme, tora ethele na tou aphairesei kai te zoe. Anazetontas enokhous kai aities, e Souki tha odegethei kateutheian sto pedio mias epikindunes makhes me magisses, bampir kai lukanthropous. O megaluteros kindunos, ostoso, apeilei ten kardia tes Souki[?] dioti einai polu duskolo na antistatheis s' auten ten ekdokhe tou Erik..."ã
àO Artour Snitsler, apo tous protous suggrapheis pou khresimopoiesan ten tekhnike tou esoterikou monologou, me te Despoinida Elze phernei me epitukhia se peras ena philodoxo egkheirema: na mas dosei mia noubela pou ektulissetai exoloklerou sto mualo tes kentrikes eroidas. Me to dieisdutiko tou blemma kai me ton diakhuto, eilikrine erotismo pou kharakterizei ta perissotera erga tou, anatemnei ton gunaikeio psukhismo me mian akribeia pou elakhistoi andres suggrapheis katapheran na petukhoun kai skiagraphei, mesa apo mia ploke pou krata liges mono ores, ten poreia mias neares gunaikas pros ten autosuneidesia.
Me te noubela aute, pou polloi theoroun os ten koruphaia tou, o Snitsler apodeiknuei oti o kosmos tou den periorizetai ste Bienne tou fin-de-siecle e tou mesopolemou. O suggrapheas proballei os prodromos ton Gallon uparxiston, eno exakolouthei na kentrizei to endiapheron, kai kurios na goeteuei ton sugkhrono anagnoste, se mia epokhe pou katakluzetai apo psukhologikes noubeles."ì
éO Entgkar Alan Poe gennetheke to 1809 ste Bostone apo goneis planodious ethopoious. Orphanepse kai apo tous duo nepio akome, kai ten kedemonia tou anelabe o euporos emporos apo to Ritsmont Tzon Alan, ston opoio o suggrapheas opheilei to mesaio tou onoma. E poiese ton sageneuse apo ta prota paidika tou khronia* molis pente eton, egraphe stikhous <>, sumphona me enan daskalo tou. Apo to 1815 os to 1820 ezese sten Agglia, opou kai teleiose to skholeio. Epistrephontas sten Amerike parakolouthese gia ligo mathemata sto Panepistemio tes Birtzinias, alla suntoma to egkateleipse. Uperetese ston amerikaniko strato, sunergasteke me polla logotekhnika periodika kai ephemerides os reporter kai demosieuse ten prote tou sulloge aphegematon to 1840. Ta pezographemata tou ekplessoun me ten poikilia tous. Plai sta diasema phantastika tou diegemata, stoikhizontai entelos diaphoretika grapta, pou o idios kharakterize <>, oi istories katharou tromou sumbadizoun me alles kathara phantastikes, ta gnesia peripeteiode aphegemata ekballoun stous prodromous ton astunomikon ki anamesa tous paremballontai kapoia keimena perigraphika kai statika, philosophikoi dialogoi kai allegories. Egrapse dokimia poietikes (Poietike arkhe kai Philosophia tes suntheses) kai polla lurika poiemata. Katexokhen suggrapheas tou <>, paradomenos ste sagene tou aphanismou, ezese opos egrapse: oriaka. Sundetheke me gunaikes pou akrobatousan sto katophli tou thanatou* e prote, e neare exadelphe tou Birtzinia Klim, ten opoia kai pantreuteke, phumatike* e deutere, e poietria kai pneumatistria Sara Elen Gouitman epises* e trite kardiake kai neurotike. Aphetheke se katakhreseis - prota sta tukhera paikhnidia kai ustera sto poto. Erototropontas sunekhos me ten katathlipse kai ten trela, prospathese na autoktonesei to 1848 kai, enan khrono argotera, stis 7 Oktobriou, pethane mesa s' enan paroxusmo alkoolikou paralerematos."ï
ìE plegomene perephaneia tes Klaires kai e anagke gia ena plousio gamo pou tha apotrepsei ten katastrophe tes oikogeneias tes, ten kanoun na prosexei to diakritiko erota tou Philippou kai na dekhtei na ginei gunaika tou, khoris ostoso na mporei na apodekhtei ten pithanoteta na agapesei ekeinon pou apokalouse "sidera".
E aletheia apokaluptetai sto Philippo molis ten prote nukhta tou gamou. E psukhroteta kai o kunismos tes Klaires ton klonizoun, apophasizei omos na antimetopisei ton egoismo tes neares gunaikas tou kai na katapherei na ten kerdisei me ton kairo. Etsi exakolouthei na ten phrontizei kai na tes sumparasteketai stis duskoles stigmes, ekhontas ostoso egkataleipsei kathe prospatheia stenoteres epikoinonias mazi tes. Aute akribos e axioprepes kai stathere sumperiphora tou, kanoun siga-siga ten Klaire na ton ektimesei, na ton zelepsei kai, telika, na ton agapesei bathia. Oso malista o Philippos sunekhizei na ten agnoei, aute e agape tes metatrepetai se paraphoro kai asugkrateto erota."ï

ì
"Ekeine ten emera, ston xethoriasmeno kathrephte ton moukhliasmenon nipteron anakalupsa ena aniaro prosopo s' ena aniaro kormi, ena parousiastiko toso adiaphoro, khoris tipote to axioprosekto, khoris katholou kharaktera, pou os ki ego o idios, epitopou, eniosa plexe. To aisthema tes metriotetas mou me kurieuse san apokalupse."
Apelpismenos apo ten tapeine tou emphanise kai ten aphaneia sten opoia pisteuei pos einai katadikasmenos, enas nearos antras apophasizei na pedexei s' enan gkremo, otan emphanizetai piso tou o diasemos ekkentrikos ekatommurioukhos kallitekhnes Zeus-Peter Lama, pou tou kanei mia protase: na ton metatrepsei se ena diethnous phemes ergo tekhnes plathontas ton ek neou, san ena anthropino agalma anotero opoioudepote allou. To mono pou tha prepei na xekhasei dia pantos, einai e anthropine upostase tou. O nearos, sigouros pos den ekhei pia tipota na khasei, dekhetai.
O Erik-Emanouel Smit, os "eikastikos logotekhnes" kai paidi tes philosophikes anazeteses, anarotietai gia te these tou "oraiou" kai tes "tekhnes" ste semerine koinonia, stenontas mia thaumaste satira-kritike tes sugkhrones piestikes kai apanthropes zoes. Anesukhetiko oso kai elkustiko, to "Otan emoun ergo tekhnes" anameignuei antikrouomena sunaisthemata pou bazoun se dokimasia tis ennoies tou "politikos orthou" kai ton "agnon protheseon" ton kallitekhnon kai ton philotekhnon opadon tous."ó
ğMia plousia kleronomos e Linet Ritzgouaie kataphernei na proselkuei ta blemmata, alla kai to misos oson briskontai guro tes. Mesa s' autous pou tha ethelan to kako tes sugkatalegetai kai e kalutere phile tes, e Zakelin nte Mpelphor, xepesmene aristokratissa. Ekhei kathe logo malista, kathos e Linet molis prosphata pantreuteke ton diko tes agapemeno. E Zakelin akolouthei tous neonumphous kai stoikheionei kathe stigme tous.
To zeugari thelontas na apallagei ap' ten okhlere parousia tes katapheugei sto polutelestato atmoploio Karnak, pou katapleei sta esukha nera tou Neilou. Dustukhos sto ploio epibainei ki enas stugeros dolophonos pou <>guro tou ptomata alla kai o Erakles Pouaro pou antimetopizei ten pio <>kai skoteine upothese tes karieras tou"÷
ôShoot/Get Treasure/Repeat is an epic cycle of plays exploring the personal and political effect of war on modern life. 
The plays that make up Shoot/Get Treasure/Repeat began life at the 2007 Edinburgh Festival Fringe as Ravenhill for Breakfast (produced
by Paines Plough), winning a Fringe First award, and the Jack Tinker
Spirit of the Fringe award. They form a collage of very different
scenes, with each taking its title from a classic work. The plays were
presented in April 2008 in various venues across London, from Notting
Hill to a Victorian warehouse in Shoreditch, via Sloane Square and the
South Bank. 
Shoot/Get Treasure/Repeatwas originally developed in association with the National Theatre Studio and Paines Plough, and was first produced as Ravenhill for Breakfast at the Traverse Theatre, Edinburgh in August 2007 by Paines Plough, with the support of David Johnson."ø
õTom Perrotta's thirtyish parents of young children are a varied and
surprising bunch. There's Todd, the handsome stay-at-home dad dubbed "The Prom
King" by the moms at the playground, and his wife, Kathy, a documentary
filmmaker envious of the connection Todd has forged with their toddler son. And
there's Sarah, a lapsed feminist surprised to find she's become a typical wife
in a traditional marriage, and her husband, Richard, who is becoming more and
more involved with an internet fantasy life than with his own wife and child.
And then there's Mary Ann, who has life all figured out, down to a scheduled
roll in the hay with her husband every Tuesday at nine P.M.
They all raise their kids in the kind of quiet suburb where nothing ever seems to happen - until one eventful summer, when a convicted child molester moves back to town, and two parents begin an affair that goes further than either of them could ever have imagined.
>Tom Perrotta is the author of several works of fiction, including Joe College and
Election, which was made into the acclaimed 1999 movies starring Reese
Witherspoon and Matthew Broderick. Perrotta has taught expository
writing at Yale and Harvard University and has been called "one of our
true genius satirists" by Mystic River author, Dennis LeHane. Newsweek
hailed him as "one of America's best-kept literary secrets...like an American
Nick Hornby." Tom lives with this wife and two children in Belmont,
Massachusetts.
Narrator George Wilson has a varied performance
background which includes more than a decade in broadcast journalism, and many
roles on stage, screen, television, and radio. A graduate of the American
Academy of Dramatic Arts. West, he was a founder of Broadway Local, an
improvisational comedy group, and has been a solo stand-up comedian. His
film work includes a lead role in the cult classic Attack of the Killer
Tomatoes. He has appeared on many popular daytime dramas. He
co-founded the award winning Soundbites, Inc., performing in over 500 editorial
cartoons for radio."ş
ûNAMED NOTABLE BOOK OF THE YEAR by Washington Post, BEST BOOKS OF THE YEAR: Kirkus Reviews, NPR, Men's Journal
A new short story collection from Luis Alberto Urrea, bestselling author of The Hummingbird's Daughter and The Devil's Highway. 
From one of America's preeminent literary voices comes a new story collection that proves once again why the writing of Luis Alberto Urrea has been called "wickedly good" (Kansas City Star), "cinematic and charged" (Cleveland Plain Dealer),and "studded with delights" (Chicago Tribune). Examining the borders between one nation and another, between one person and another, Urrea reveals his mastery of the short form. This collection includes the Edgar-award winning "Amapola" and his now-classic "Bid Farewell to Her Many Horses," which had the honor of being chosen for NPR's "Selected Shorts" not once but twice.
Suffused with wanderlust, compassion, and no small amount of rock and roll, THE WATER MUSEUM is a collection that confirms Luis Alberto Urrea as an American master."€
ıBestselling writer Daniel Abraham and acclaimed illustrator Tommy Patterson bring their stunning graphic-novel adaptation of George R. R. Martin's classic A Game of Thronesto a stunning finish that merits a place alongside the majestic original on the bookshelf of every fantasy fan.
The death of King Robert Baratheon and the imprisonment of his Hand, Lord Eddard Stark of Winterfell, has set the great houses of Westeros at one another's throats.
In Winterfell, Eddard's eldest son and heir, Robb Stark, has gathered an army and is pushing south, determined to free his father. Along the way, he pledges to marry the daughter of Lord Walder Frey in exchange for a military advantage that allows him to capture Jaime Lannister--a powerful bargaining chip to ensure Lord Eddard's safe release. But it is one thing to capture the Kingslayer and quite another to hold him.
Meanwhile, in King's Landing, young King Joffrey has other ideas than an exchange of prisoners. Ignoring the advice of his mother, Queen Cersei, he throws oil on the flames of conflict and ignites a conflagration that seems likely to consume not only the Starks but all of Westeros--unless Tyrion Lannister, the Imp, can bring the mad boy-king to heel.
Beyond the Wall, greater dangers are brewing, as a winter as brutal as any in history approaches, bringing with it unnatural creatures out of legend. There, Eddard's bastard, Jon Snow, must decide once and for all where his loyalties lie.
And across the Narrow Sea, Daenerys Targaryen will learn the true measure of grief--and emerge from its fiery depths transformed, hardened, and ready to claim what is hers by right: the Iron Throne."	333333@"	Ház®G@"	\Âõ(\@"	ffffff@"	q=
